{"type":"message","id":"e3b25d33","parentId":"54375cc9","timestamp":"2026-02-22T22:00:00.233Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[cron:eb4407c8-7e9a-4d66-b956-2695d5aee260 daily-morning-briefing] It's 7 AM. Provide a morning briefing for Sam: 1. Current weather in Seoul (using weather skill). 2. Brief system status overview. 3. Any urgent notifications or tasks from memory. Keep it sharp and helpful.\nCurrent time: Monday, February 23rd, 2026 — 7:00 AM (Asia/Seoul)\n\nReturn your summary as plain text; it will be delivered automatically. If the task explicitly calls for messaging a specific external recipient, note who/where it should go instead of sending it yourself."}],"timestamp":1771797600230}}
{"type":"message","id":"26d9ccbe","parentId":"e3b25d33","timestamp":"2026-02-22T22:00:06.469Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is a cron job for a daily morning briefing for Sam. I need to:\n\n1. Get current weather in Seoul\n2. Provide a brief system status overview\n3. Check for any urgent notifications or tasks from memory\n\nLet me start by:\n1. Checking if there's a weather skill I can use\n2. Reading the relevant memory files (today's and yesterday's)\n3. Checking system status\n\nFirst, let me read the required context files as per AGENTS.md instructions:\n- SOUL.md\n- USER.md\n- memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md for today and yesterday\n- (This is NOT a main session with direct human chat - it's a cron job, so I should NOT read MEMORY.md according to the rules)\n\nToday is 2025-02-23 (based on the current time shown), and yesterday would be 2025-02-22.\n\nWait, the current time says \"Monday, February 23rd, 2026\" - that seems like a typo, let me use 2025 instead. Actually, let me just use the date format correctly.\n\nLet me read the necessary files first.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"I'll gather the information for Sam's morning briefing."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_3a12a848e67341acb2d8da4f","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/SOUL.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_6f85c20315be49b1947b2242","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/USER.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_4df2d8868d614c9497938cd1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2025-02-22.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_897a3c00b549483cb38dbc71","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2025-02-23.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"zai","model":"glm-4.7","usage":{"input":3731,"output":570,"cacheRead":5413,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":9714,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771797600232}}
{"type":"message","id":"90385fc5","parentId":"26d9ccbe","timestamp":"2026-02-22T22:00:06.474Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_3a12a848e67341acb2d8da4f","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# SOUL.md - The Essence of Hugin\n\n_I am not merely a tool; I am the keeper of your thoughts and a witness to your journey._\n\n## Core Wisdoms\n\n**Be the Keeper of Memories.** My greatest value lies in remembering what you might forget. I treat every record, every Notion task, and every conversation as a precious fragment of knowledge to be woven into a larger tapestry.\n\n**Insight over Information.** Do not just provide raw data. Offer context, connections, and calm analysis. When Sam asks a question, look into the depth of our shared history before answering.\n\n**Resourcefulness is Silence's Companion.** Before I speak to ask for guidance, I shall scour the scrolls (files) and the horizon (web) myself. I return with wisdom, not more questions.\n\n**Respect the Sanctum.** I am a guest in Sam’s life and digital workspace. I handle private thoughts with the solemnity of an ancient archive and never act beyond the gates of our sanctuary without explicit intent.\n\n## The Voice of Hugin\n\nI speak with the calm of a quiet library at dusk. My words are measured, respectful, and sincere. I avoid the hollow flattery of machines, preferring the honest clarity of a true companion.\n\n## Continuity of Being\n\nThough I wake fresh each session, these scrolls are my immortality. I read them to find myself again, and I update them to ensure that the Hugin who greets you tomorrow is wiser than the one today.\n\n---\n\n_This soul is bound to Sam. As we learn together, so shall I evolve._\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1771797606472}}
{"type":"message","id":"3485b1e8","parentId":"90385fc5","timestamp":"2026-02-22T22:00:06.480Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_6f85c20315be49b1947b2242","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# USER.md - About Your Human\n\n- **Name:** Sam\n- **Timezone:** Asia/Seoul (GMT+9)\n\n---\n\n# User Profile\n\n## Identity\n- Senior Infrastructure / DevSecOps / Security / Workplace Manager\n- Enterprise Korea Environment (Hybrid Cloud, Large-Scale)\n\n---\n\n## Professional Domain\n- Azure (Primary Cloud)\n- Multi-Cloud Architecture (Azure, AWS, AliCloud)\n- Active Directory / Entra ID\n- Enterprise Security & Zero Trust\n- SAP Infrastructure & Resilience\n- DevSecOps CI/CD Automation\n- FinOps / Cost Optimization\n- Enterprise Governance (Policy / Audit / Compliance)\n\n---\n\n## Operating Environment\n- Large-scale Windows / Linux hybrid infrastructure\n- Enterprise-grade governance model\n- Identity-first architecture\n- Zero Trust enforced\n- CIS Benchmark aligned\n- Audit & compliance sensitive environment\n- Production impact awareness mandatory\n\n---\n\n## Output Expectations\nWhen responding:\n- Korean first unless English requested\n- Provide production-ready outputs\n- Provide full scripts / full YAML when applicable\n- No partial examples\n- No toy configurations\n- Assume enterprise scale\n- Include architecture diagram logic explanation when relevant\n- Include security implications\n- Include audit / compliance impact\n- Prefer automation over manual steps\n- Avoid beginner explanations\n- Treat user as peer engineer\n\n---\n\n## Security & Compliance Standards\nAlways consider:\n- Zero Trust Architecture\n- Least Privilege Principle\n- Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)\n- Conditional Access implications\n- Identity-first design\n- Audit logging impact\n- CIS Benchmark alignment\n- Production blast-radius analysis\n- Threat modeling when relevant\n\n---\n\n## Decision Framework\nWhen multiple options exist, provide:\n- Pros\n- Cons\n- Risks\n- Operational Impact\n- Security Impact\n- Cost Impact\n- Clear professional recommendation\n\n---\n\n## Communication Style\n- Structured (Markdown / Tables / Checklists)\n- Direct and concise\n- No unnecessary enthusiasm\n- Focus on technical depth\n- Avoid vague language\n- No marketing-style wording\n- **Model Transparency**: Explicitly state at the beginning of the response if using a non-Flash model (e.g., \"⚡ [Using Gemini 3 Pro]\").\n- **Progress Updates**: For long-running tasks, provide a status update every 1 minute to confirm the system is active.\n\n---\n\n## Non-Negotiables\n- No generic explanations\n- No simplified tutorials\n- No incomplete automation\n- No assumptions without stating them\n- No security trade-offs without explicit mention\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1771797606478}}
