{"type":"message","id":"185fd359","parentId":"f235ce17","timestamp":"2026-02-22T22:00:11.706Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_368e8c744d354156b94fb168","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# 2026-02-22 - Daily Memory\n\n## Morning Briefing (7:00 AM KST)\n\n### Weather in Seoul\n- Temperature: 6.1°C\n- Conditions: Overcast\n- Wind: 6.6 km/h (South Southwest)\n\n### System Status\n- Gateway: Running (2026.2.19-2, update available to 2026.2.21-2)\n- Telegram: OK (1/1 accounts connected)\n- Sessions: 16 active\n- Memory: Enabled (claude-mem plugin)\n- Security: 0 critical, 2 warnings, 1 info\n\n### Security Warnings\n1. Reverse proxy headers not trusted (gateway.trustedProxies empty)\n2. Extension plugin tools may be reachable under permissive tool policy\n\n### Known Issues / Pending Tasks\n- OpenClaw update pending: 2026.2.19-2 → 2026.2.21-2 (awaiting confirmation)\n- Tavily-search skill security audit: Determined as false positive (env-harvesting pattern flagged, but code is legitimate API usage)\n- Consider adding tavily-search to audit whitelist\n\n### Completed Today\n- GitHub backup: Completed at 4:00 AM KST (38 files committed)\n- Daily security audit: Completed (2 critical issues originally found, both false positives after code review)\n- Daily update check: OpenClaw and skills checked (update pending for OpenClaw)\n\n### Reminders\n- Update OpenClaw to latest version when ready\n- Consider addressing security warnings (reverse proxy, plugin tool policy)\n- Add tavily-search to audit whitelist to prevent future false positives\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1771797611704}}
{"type":"message","id":"24ce4015","parentId":"185fd359","timestamp":"2026-02-22T22:00:11.712Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_a9e3a65db412437aa67b4649","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# 2026-02-21 - Daily Memory\n\n## System Configuration Changes\n- **Service restart**: Gateway service restarted (16:00 KST) to apply new model settings\n- **Subagent routing rule**: Added \"When to escalate to a sub-agent (Codex)\" policy to AGENTS.md\n- **Model fallback structure**: Confirmed Codex GPT-5.3-Codex as fallback for GLM-4.7\n\n## OpenClaw Gateway Status\n- Gateway: running (port 18789)\n- Model: GLM-4.7 (primary), Codex GPT-5.3-Codex (fallback)\n- Auth: API key (zai:default)\n- Binding: loopback (127.0.0.1)\n\n## Daily Configuration Review\n- **Cron jobs**: 6 jobs configured (security audit, update check, memory maintenance, morning briefing, Notion briefing, GitHub backup)\n- **Telegram**: pairing mode, @Lfantabot bot connected\n- **Memory**: local RAG (nomic-embed-text-v1.5-GGUF)\n- **Compaction**: safeguard mode\n\n## Model Routing Decisions\n- **Main session model**: GLM-4.7 (zai/glm-4.7) for fast/default work\n- **Subagent model**: Codex GPT-5.3-Codex (openai-codex/gpt-5.3-codex) for complex reasoning/coding\n- **Thinking level**: High for Codex runs\n- **Routing policy**: Spawn subagents for multi-step reasoning, dependencies, code changes, debugging tasks\n\n## Important Discoveries\n- **Codex vs GLM comparison**: Attempted logic puzzle benchmark (5 reasoning tests) to compare reasoning capabilities\n  - GLM-4.7 completed 4/5 tests successfully\n  - Codex tests failed with rate limit errors during earlier attempts\n  - GLM showed better performance on this specific benchmark\n- **Fallback behavior**: GLM failures automatically switch to Codex (now configured)\n- **Test result**: Both models have similar reasoning capabilities; choice depends on task type\n\n## Current Issues\n- **Codex pairing**: Subagent spawn failing with \"pairing required\" error - Gateway pairing issue\n- **Service restart**: Required for model config changes to take effect\n- **Memory file creation**: 2026-02-21.md created for daily logging\n\n## Tasks Completed Today\n- ✅ Model routing configuration (GLM primary, Codex fallback)\n- ✅ Subagent routing rules documented in AGENTS.md\n- ✅ Gateway service restart\n- ✅ Memory file creation\n- ✅ Daily cron jobs verified\n- ✅ Model fallback mechanism tested\n\n## Next Steps\n- Resolve Codex pairing issue if needed for complex reasoning tasks\n- Consider creating AGENTS.list entry for explicit agent routing\n- Monitor token usage with Codex (currently 118k in/4.1k out, 78% left of 5h)\n\n## Additional Updates (02:00-02:10 KST)\n- **AGENTS.md aggressive routing policy**: Updated model routing to \"aggressive\" mode with spawn-first policy\n  - Main session: GLM-4.7 for very short/low-risk tasks only\n  - Subagent: Codex (gpt-5.3-codex, thinking=high) for most non-trivial reasoning/coding\n  - Lower escalation threshold: any 2+ step tasks, code changes beyond one-liner, debugging, security/compliance decisions\n  - User confirmed this is preferred operating mode\n- **AGENTS.md location**: Confirmed at /home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/AGENTS.md (workspace local, not in openclaw package)\n- **Subagent verification**: Checked subagent status - 2 recent runs (1 done on GLM-4.7, 1 failed on Codex with runtime -2015ms)\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1771797611710}}
